From 9310f27fc7ba768bbab3c9f567c8a7ddc0862a1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 13:01:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] agentHost: mark a turn interrupted by a host crash on
 restore

Copilot already reports a turn that was in flight when the host died,
because its SDK event log records abort and idle events. Claude's
transcript carries no result marker, so its replay closed such a turn
as complete or cancelled and the user was never told the request did
not finish. Codex maps an in-progress rollout to a complete turn as
well.

Add a host-owned interruptedTurn chat contribution. On dispatch it
records the open turn (id and start time) in the chat database's
metadata when a turn starts or resumes, and clears it when the turn
completes, is cancelled, errors, or the chat is truncated. On hydrate
it reads the marker, clears it so later getMessages calls do not
re-mark, and replaces the trailing restored turn with an error turn
carrying a non-resumable executionInterrupted part, using the same
message Copilot shows. The trailing turn is matched by id, or by start
time for providers that re-key turns on replay, with a one second
tolerance because Codex persists start times in whole seconds. A turn
already restored as an error is left alone, so Copilot is unaffected,
and subagent chats and chats with a live turn are skipped.
