From f78cd4a433d79b13c4aa24b5060e5b899b91e883 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:22:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] agentHost: keep interrupted marking when clearing the
 marker fails

Clearing the open-turn marker on hydrate is best effort, but it ran
before the trailing turn was marked and inside the same try block, so a
transient failure of that write threw past the marking and returned the
provider's turn unchanged. The database had already been read
successfully and the turn genuinely was interrupted, so the user was
shown a turn that falsely reads as complete: the exact bug this
contribution exists to prevent. Recovering the turn and cleaning up the
marker are independent, so compute the marked turns first and clear in
a helper that logs and swallows its own failure.

A marker that survives a failed clear is read again by the next
hydrate, which marks the same turn again. That is acceptable and needs
no extra guard. The provider replays the same unmarked turns, so the
second pass produces the same single error part rather than a second
one, and a list that already carries the error is left alone by the
existing check for an already errored trailing turn. The marker is also
self healing: any later turn on that chat overwrites it on start and
clears it on completion.
